{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019WwuneT2aLZAzRb2Hu9wfP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for all planned experiments in the experiment plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to provide specific predicted metrics with rationales for each experiment.\n\nLet me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate plausible \"best\" tier results based on:\n1. The best tier definition (repo-level validates complexity-dependent advantage; diagnostic re-repair works; full story holds)\n2. The key metric ranges defined for best tier\n3. Already completed experiment results (mvp-b-train CLS F1 ~87.1/87.9, cwm-baseline F1 ~87.3/87.7 — essentially equivalent)\n\n\n4. The narrative direction\n\nNow I'm listing out all the planned experiments to work through systematically: multi-seed validation, trace-then-judge ablation, trajectory-level fine-tuned baseline, scaling to 8B, downstream re-repair, per-test failure prediction quality, stratified oracle analysis, block correlation validation, and a few others that got cut off.\n\nLet me think through what success looks like for each experiment. For the multi-seed core validation, I'm aiming for standard deviation under 0.5 percentage points with a tight range around 0.1-0.4pp—this would confirm the null result is genuinely robust. The CLS and CWM models should both hit around 87 F1 with minimal variance, showing the gap between them is just noise. For the trace-then-judge ablation, I'm expecting the performance drop to fall somewhere between -2.0 and 0.0 percentage points.\n\nThe trace-then-judge approach should show a slight degradation or equivalence to direct classification, somewhere around -1.0 to -1.5pp, which would confirm that reformulation rather than reasoning is what's driving the improvements. Trajectory-level fine-tuning should demonstrate decent performance but with some loss of per-test granularity—the trajectory accuracy should be comparable to aggregated per-test results while still providing useful diagnostic information. At the 8B model size, both approaches should improve by roughly 1-2 percentage points while keeping the gap under 0.5pp. The diagnostic repair experiment should show around 10-12% improvement in the resolution delta. I'm also looking at precision and recall metrics for failure detection, and expecting the oracle advantage to concentrate in instances with two or more trajectories.\n\nNow I'm examining the empirical block correlations, which should fall in the 0.25-0.35 range and align more closely with the block model. The SWE-bench per-test dataset construction and success metrics are part of the evaluation framework. For repo-level training, I'm expecting the CLS F1 to reach around 80 while CWM F1 sits around 70, giving roughly a 10 percentage point gap. The zero-shot LLM judge baseline should underperform the fine-tuned version, and majority voting over per-test predictions should provide only marginal gains. I'm going to organize all these findings into a structured format with detailed rationales.\n\nLooking at what's actually planned versus already completed, I should focus only on the experiments marked as planned or still in preparation. That means filtering out oracle-total-validated and cwm-baseline since those are done. Let me identify the full set of planned experiments to cover comprehensively with results and visualizations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22222,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22222},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a2813a-ede9-44c9-b128-12e272d1c1ce","uuid":"0d4df1ba-2726-48fc-9102-4b37fd953919"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019WwuneT2aLZAzRb2Hu9wfP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完整成立。Function-level null result 通过 multi-seed 确认为 robust，\n  trace-then-judge 证明优势来自 reformulation 而非显式推理。Repo-level 实验中 CWM \n  因 token-budget exhaustion 和 string-value 错误显著落后 classification（~10pp gap），\n  验证 complexity-dependent advantage。Diagnostic re-repair 带来 ~10% resolve rate 提升，\n  block-correlated error structure 实证确认。三条 claim 全部成立，投稿 EMNLP 2026 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification (mvp-b) 和 CWM baseline 各跑 seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean ± std F1，\n      paired bootstrap CI 检验显著性。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.05\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.22\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.88\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.18\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.28\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.31\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.65\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 0.27\n      f1_gap_cls_minus_cwm_pass: -0.23\n      f1_gap_cls_minus_cwm_fail: 0.23\n      paired_bootstrap_p_value: 0.71\n      overlap_95ci: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Function-level 任务的 execution output 短（通常 <20 tokens），CWM 的 token-budget \n      和 string-value 失败模式几乎不触发（exact_match 84% 已经很高）。两种 formulation \n      在信息论上等价：pass/fail 是 output 的确定性函数，模型容量足以学到等效映射。\n      三个 seed 的 std 在 0.2-0.3pp 范围内，符合 4B LoRA 在 ~1890 测试样本上的 \n      expected sampling variance（binomial SE ≈ 0.7pp，LoRA init variance 贡献 ~0.2pp）。\n      p=0.71 远高于 0.05，确认 null result 不是单次运气。这为 repo-level 的 \n      complexity-dependent advantage 提供干净的 baseline：function-level 等价是前提。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"0\", \"86.8\", \"88.1\", \"87.3\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"1\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.6\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"42\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"mean±std\", \"87.05±0.22\", \"87.88±0.18\", \"87.47±0.13\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"0\", \"86.9\", \"87.4\", \"87.1\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"1\", \"87.6\", \"87.9\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"42\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"mean±std\", \"87.28±0.31\", \"87.65±0.27\", \"87.47±0.29\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing F1 distribution across 3 seeds for CLS vs CWM, 95% CI heavily overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Null result robust：三种子方差 <0.5pp，bootstrap CI 完全重叠。\n      这排除了 \"classification trivially easier\" 的 reviewer concern——\n      在 function-level，两种 formulation 的信息瓶颈相同。\n      CWM 略高的 std（0.31 vs 0.22）暗示 generation 对初始化更敏感，\n      但差异不显著。该结果直接支撑 Claim 1 的前半部分。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单一 Qwen3-4B 模型训练为先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。\n      与直接 classification 对比，检验显式推理是否有帮助。\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 86.1\n      ttj_fail_f1: 86.4\n      ttj_accuracy: 86.2\n      ttj_minus_direct_pass_f1: -0.95\n      ttj_minus_direct_fail_f1: -1.49\n      trace_avg_tokens: 47.3\n      unparseable_rate_pct: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-judge 要求模型在同一 forward pass 中既做 execution reasoning \n      又做 classification。对 4B 参数模型，额外的 trace generation 引入两个负面效应：\n      (1) LoRA capacity 分流——部分参数用于学习 trace 的 surface form 而非 \n      code-test 语义对齐；(2) error propagation——trace 中的推理错误（如变量值 \n      跟踪错误）可能污染后续 pass/fail 判断。在 function-level 这种 \"答案明确\" \n      的设置下，explicit reasoning 不提供额外信息增益（模型已能从 code+test \n      直接推断结果），反而增加了 sequence length 和 loss 分配的竞争。\n      预测 F1 下降 ~1pp，在 best tier 范围 [-2.0, 0.0] 内。\n      这直接证明 reformulation（将 generation 转为 classification）才是关键驱动力，\n      而非 \"跳过推理\" 这一表面简化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"Avg Output Tokens\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct Classification\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\", \"1\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge\", \"86.1\", \"86.4\", \"86.2\", \"48.3\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\", \"34.7\"]\n          - [\"Δ (TtJ − Direct)\", \"-1.0\", \"-1.5\", \"-1.3\", \"+47.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing three methods (Direct CLS, TtJ, CWM) on Pass/Fail F1, showing TtJ slightly below both others\"\n      - \"Example trace outputs showing correct reasoning leading to correct verdict vs incorrect variable tracking leading to wrong verdict\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-judge ≤ direct classification，确认 reformulation \n      而非 explicit reasoning 是 classification 的优势来源。\n      这回应了 \"classification 只是跳过了有用的推理步骤\" 的潜在质疑——\n      加回推理步骤反而有害。值得注意的是 CWM 也不输于 TtJ，\n      说明 CWM 的 generation 过程本身隐含了 execution reasoning，\n      但在 function-level 这一优势被 short output 的 trivial prediction 抵消。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练为预测 resolved/unresolved（trajectory-level），\n      用 aggregated test labels 构造数据。隔离 granularity effect。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 85.3\n      traj_resolved_f1: 84.1\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 86.2\n      traj_resolved_precision: 82.7\n      traj_resolved_recall: 85.5\n      traj_unresolved_precision: 87.4\n      traj_unresolved_recall: 85.1\n      per_test_aggregated_traj_accuracy: 86.8\n      granularity_gap_pct: 1.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 模型将所有 tests 拼接为单一输入，预测 binary resolved/unresolved。\n      相比 per-test 模型，它面临两个劣势：(1) 输入长度显著增加（多个 test 拼接），\n      稀释了对单个 test 的注意力；(2) label 是 all-or-nothing（任一 test fail 则 \n      unresolved），丢失了 \"哪个 test 失败\" 的细粒度信号。在 function-level 数据中 \n      多数 problem 只有 1-3 个 test，所以劣势不大（~1.5pp gap）。但关键发现是 \n      per-test 模型通过 aggregation（majority vote over per-test predictions）可以 \n      recover trajectory-level 判断，反之不行——trajectory-level 无法提供 diagnostic \n      信号。这为 Claim 2 提供了 granularity 的信息论论证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Per-Test vs Trajectory-Level Granularity\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Task\", \"Accuracy\", \"Resolved F1\", \"Unresolved F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Per-Test CLS\", \"per-test pass/fail\", \"87.5\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Per-Test CLS → aggregated\", \"trajectory resolved\", \"86.8\", \"85.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"Trajectory-Level\", \"trajectory resolved\", \"85.3\", \"84.1\", \"86.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diagram showing information flow: per-test → aggregate = trajectory, but trajectory ↛ per-test\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test 模型 aggregated 后比直接训练的 trajectory-level 模型高 1.5pp，\n      证明细粒度 supervision 提供了更好的学习信号。更重要的是 per-test \n      是 strictly more informative：可以 aggregate 到 trajectory-level，\n      还能提供 diagnostic 信息，而 trajectory-level 无法分解。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      将 classification 和 CWM 模型从 4B 扩展到 8B，检验 function-level \n      equivalence 是否在更大模型上依然成立。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.4\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 89.7\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.1\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 89.5\n      cls_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.2\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.0\n      gap_8b_cls_minus_cwm: 0.2\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型在 function-level 上两种 formulation 均提升 ~2pp（log-linear scaling），\n      但 gap 依然 <0.5pp。原因同 multi-seed：function-level output 短，CWM 的 \n      failure modes 不触发。8B 的额外 capacity 均匀地提升了 code semantics 理解，\n      两种 formulation 同等受益。exact_match 从 84% 提升到 87%，说明更大模型 \n      能更精确地预测 output string，但这在 function-level 上不转化为 F1 优势。\n      这个结果强化了 \"gap 是 complexity-dependent 而非 capacity-dependent\" 的论点——\n      需要 repo-level 的复杂 output 才能拉开差距。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Model Size Scaling\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"CWM Exact Match\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"4B\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"8B\", \"89.4\", \"90.1\", \"89.7\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"4B\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\", \"84.0%\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"8B\", \"89.1\", \"89.8\", \"89.5\", \"87.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=model size (4B, 8B), y=F1, two lines (CLS, CWM) nearly parallel and overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Function-level equivalence 在 8B 维持（gap 0.2pp），排除了 \n      \"4B 太小所以 CWM 被 capacity bottleneck 惩罚\" 的替代解释。\n      Scaling 曲线几乎平行，表明两种 formulation 的 scaling exponent 一致。\n      结合 repo-level 结果（gap ~10pp），这证明 advantage 的触发条件是 \n      task complexity 而非 model capacity。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      在 200 个 SWE-bench 实例上对比：repair agent + per-test failure predictions \n      vs repair agent + trajectory-level binary only。衡量 resolve rate 差异。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 28.5\n      diagnostic_resolve_rate_pct: 38.0\n      resolve_delta_pct: 9.5\n      resolve_delta_ci_95: [5.2, 13.8]\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 32\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 13\n      net_improvement_instances: 19\n      avg_repair_iterations_baseline: 3.2\n      avg_repair_iterations_diagnostic: 2.4\n      diagnostic_precision_on_helped: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-test failure predictions 提供了 \"哪个 test 失败\" 的 targeted 信息，\n      使 repair agent 能聚焦于特定失败点而非盲目搜索。在 best tier 下预测 \n      ~9.5% 的 resolve rate 提升（range [5, 15]）。提升来源：(1) 多 F2P test \n      实例中，agent 知道具体失败 test 后可优先修复最关键的失败；(2) 减少了 \n      repair iteration 次数（3.2 → 2.4），因为 diagnostic 信号缩小了搜索空间。\n      有 13 个实例 diagnostic 反而有害，主要因 false positive failure predictions \n      误导 agent 去修复没有 broken 的部分。但 net 正向（19 instances），\n      且 95% CI 不包含 0，统计显著。这直接验证了 Claim 2。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"Avg Iterations\", \"N\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline (binary only)\", \"28.5%\", \"3.2\", \"200\"]\n          - [\"+ Diagnostic per-test\", \"38.0%\", \"2.4\", \"200\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+9.5% [5.2, 13.8]\", \"-0.8\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 8: Diagnostic Impact Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"Count\", \"Pct\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Diagnostic helped (unresolved → resolved)\", \"32\", \"16.0%\"]\n          - [\"Diagnostic hurt (resolved → unresolved)\", \"13\", \"6.5%\"]\n          - [\"No change\", \"155\", \"77.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: baseline vs diagnostic resolve rates, broken down by F2P test count (T=1, T≥2)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=per-test prediction accuracy on instance, y=whether diagnostic helped\"\n    analysis: >\n      9.5% resolve rate 提升统计显著（CI 不含 0）。提升集中在 T≥2 实例 \n      （与 Claim 3 oracle 分析一致）。Iteration 减少 25% 意味着即使 \n      resolve rate 不变，diagnostic 也有 efficiency value。\n      Hurt cases 主要源于 false positive predictions（precision ~78%），\n      提示 per-test accuracy 仍有改善空间。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall，\n      评估 diagnostic 信号质量（不依赖下游执行）。\n    expected_results:\n      failure_precision: 0.876\n      failure_recall: 0.882\n      failure_f1: 0.879\n      pass_precision: 0.874\n      pass_recall: 0.868\n      pass_f1: 0.871\n      macro_f1: 0.875\n      per_problem_perfect_prediction_rate: 0.71\n      per_problem_at_least_one_correct_fail: 0.93\n      confusion_matrix: {TP: 835, FP: 118, FN: 117, TN: 820}\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些数字直接来自 mvp-b-train 的已有结果（pass F1 87.1, fail F1 87.9），\n      此实验是将其分解为 per-problem 粒度的分析。71% 的 problem 所有 test \n      prediction 完全正确——这些 instance 的 diagnostic 信号完全可靠。\n      93% 的 problem 至少有一个 failing test 被正确识别——即使不完美，\n      diagnostic 信号仍有 partial value。Failure precision 87.6% 意味着 \n      每 8 个 predicted-fail 中约 1 个是 false alarm，这与 re-repair 实验中 \n      diagnostic hurt 的比例一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Per-Test Diagnostic Signal Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Failure Precision\", \"0.876\"]\n          - [\"Failure Recall\", \"0.882\"]\n          - [\"Per-problem perfect prediction\", \"71%\"]\n          - [\"Per-problem ≥1 correct fail detected\", \"93%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-recall curve for failure detection at different classification thresholds\"\n      - \"Histogram of per-problem prediction accuracy (fraction of tests correctly predicted)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic 信号质量足以支撑 downstream re-repair：93% 的 problem \n      至少检测到一个真正的 failing test。Per-problem perfect prediction \n      71% 设定了 diagnostic re-repair 的理论上限——对这些 instance，\n      agent 获得完美的 test-level 指引。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T=3+) 分层的 oracle 分析，\n      展示 per-test advantage 集中在 multi-test 实例。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 15.8\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.5\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.298\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.441\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.102\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.219\n    result_rationale: >\n      Oracle simulation 的数学结构决定了 per-test advantage 随 T 单调递增。\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory-level 信息论等价（只有一个 test，\n      pass/fail = resolved/unresolved），advantage 仅来自 tie-breaking \n      在 block-correlated 场景下的微小收益（~0.11）。T=2 时 per-test \n      可以区分 \"两个 test 都 fail\" vs \"一个 pass 一个 fail\"，提供了 \n      trajectory-level 无法获得的额外信息，advantage 跳升至 ~0.19/0.36。\n      T≥3 进一步放大。关键 insight：虽然 T≥2 只占 31.3% 的 SWE-bench 实例，\n      但这些实例贡献了绝大部分 per-test advantage。这提供了 practical \n      decision framework：per-test simulation 值得部署在 multi-test 实例上。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Per-Test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"IID Advantage\", \"Block Advantage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"0.020\", \"0.109\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"15.8%\", \"0.185\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15.5%\", \"0.298\", \"0.441\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", \"0.102\", \"0.219\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: x=T bucket, y=advantage, two bars per group (IID, Block)\"\n      - \"Cumulative advantage curve: x=instances sorted by T descending, y=cumulative per-test advantage contribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      T≥2 实例虽然只占 31.3%，但在 block model 下贡献了 \n      (0.362×15.8 + 0.441×15.5) / (0.219×100) ≈ 57% 的总 advantage。\n      这为 selective deployment 提供了明确的 decision boundary：\n      对 T=1 实例可以用 trajectory-level（更简单），\n      对 T≥2 实例部署 per-test verification。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练模型的 test-level predictions 中测量实际 error correlation structure，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-correlated simulation 模型对比。\n    expected_results:\n      empirical_within_instance_error_corr: 0.28\n      iid_model_expected_corr: 0.0\n      block_model_fitted_corr: 0.25\n      block_model_r_squared: 0.87\n      iid_model_r_squared: 0.43\n      residual_heterogeneity: 0.04\n      n_instances_measured: 350\n    result_rationale: >\n      同一 problem_id 下的 tests 共享 code context，模型对该 code 的 \n      \"理解深度\" 产生 instance-level 的 systematic error component。\n      如果模型对某段代码的语义理解有偏差，该 problem 下所有 test 的 \n      prediction 都会系统性偏移——这正是 block correlation 的来源。\n      r=0.28 在 best tier range [0.15, 0.4] 内，表明真实 error structure \n      显著非 i.i.d.（i.i.d. R²=0.43 远低于 block R²=0.87）。\n      Block model 能解释 87% 的 variance，验证了 oracle simulation \n      中使用 block model 的假设。Residual heterogeneity 0.04 表明 \n      block model 不完美但已足够好。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Error Correlation Model Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Expected ρ\", \"Observed ρ\", \"R²\", \"AIC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"I.I.D.\", \"0.00\", \"—\", \"0.43\", \"1247\"]\n          - [\"Block-Correlated\", \"0.25\", \"0.28\", \"0.87\", \"892\"]\n          - [\"Empirical\", \"—\", \"0.28\", \"1.00\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=instance ID (sorted by per-instance error rate), y=per-test error indicator, showing clustering within instances\"\n      - \"QQ plot comparing empirical advantage distribution against IID and block simulation predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Empirical r=0.28 接近 block model 的 fitted r=0.25，远离 i.i.d. 的 0.0。\n      Block model R²=0.87 vs i.i.d. R²=0.43，AIC 差异 355 点，\n      提供了强有力的 model selection 证据。这验证了 oracle simulation \n      的核心假设，也解释了为什么 per-test advantage 在实践中 \n      比 i.i.d. 预测更大。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Per-Test Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels，\n      构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_instances: 467\n      failed_docker_instances: 33\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 89280\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 12.0\n      avg_f2p_tests: 2.8\n      avg_p2p_tests: 9.2\n      label_distribution_pass_pct: 73.5\n      label_distribution_fail_pct: 26.5\n      median_test_code_tokens: 847\n      median_patch_code_tokens: 312\n      docker_total_cpu_hours: 19.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      500 个 SWE-bench Verified 实例中 ~93% 成功提取 per-test labels，\n      33 个失败主要因 Docker 环境问题（依赖版本冲突、timeout）。\n      每个 instance 平均 12 个 test（2.8 F2P + 9.2 P2P），16 个 candidates \n      产生 ~89K 对 (code, test, label)。Pass 率 73.5% 反映了大多数 candidate \n      能通过大多数 P2P tests 但 fail 一些 F2P tests。这个数据集的 class \n      imbalance（73.5/26.5）比 function-level（~52/48）更极端，\n      会成为 repo-level training 的挑战。CPU 消耗 ~19h 符合 16 parallel \n      containers 的预算。该数据集本身是 resource contribution。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", \"467\"]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", \"16\"]\n          - [\"Total (code, test, label) pairs\", \"89,280\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests / instance\", \"2.8\"]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests / instance\", \"9.2\"]\n          - [\"Pass/Fail ratio\", \"73.5% / 26.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of test count distribution across instances\"\n      - \"Histogram of F2P vs P2P test count distribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集成功构建，467 instances 足以做 train/val/test split（如 350/50/67）。\n      Class imbalance 提示 repo-level training 需要 weighted loss 或 \n      oversampling 策略。F2P 平均 2.8 tests 意味着 31% 多 F2P test 实例 \n      的 oracle 分析在此数据上直接适用。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training & Evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上 fine-tune Qwen3-4B/8B 做 repo-level \n      per-test classification 和 CWM generation，评估 complexity-dependent advantage。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_pass_f1: 78.3\n      cls_4b_fail_f1: 72.1\n      cls_4b_accuracy: 76.2\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 81.5\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 75.8\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 79.4\n      cwm_4b_pass_f1: 69.8\n      cwm_4b_fail_f1: 63.4\n      cwm_4b_accuracy: 67.5\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 73.2\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 67.1\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 71.0\n      repo_f1_gap_4b_cls_minus_cwm: 8.7\n      repo_f1_gap_8b_cls_minus_cwm: 8.4\n      cwm_4b_exact_match: 31.2\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 42.7\n      cwm_token_budget_exhaustion_pct: 23.5\n      cwm_string_value_error_pct: 18.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level 是整个 paper story 的关键验证点。Classification 在 repo-level \n      仍然只需预测 1 token (pass/fail)，但 CWM 现在需要预测长 execution output \n      （median ~847 tokens 的 test 产生更长的 output）。两个 failure modes 爆发：\n      (1) Token-budget exhaustion（23.5%）：output 超过 generation context window \n      被截断，导致 exact match 失败，模型被迫在 truncated output 上做判断；\n      (2) String-value prediction errors（18.3%）：repo-level output 包含路径、\n      hash、timestamp 等不可预测的 string values，即使逻辑正确也会 mismatch。\n      两者合计影响 ~40% 的 test cases，直接解释了 CWM 的 ~8.5pp F1 drop。\n      Classification 不受这些 failure modes 影响——它只需从 code+test 的语义 \n      推断 pass/fail，不需要重建 output string。8B 模型缩小了部分差距 \n      （exact match 31.2% → 42.7%），但 gap 仍 >8pp，证明这不是 capacity 问题 \n      而是 formulation 的 fundamental limitation。\n      cls_pass_f1 在 [75, 85] range 内（78.3/81.5），repo_f1_gap 在 [5, 15] \n      range 内（8.7/8.4），完全符合 best tier 定义。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Repo-Level Classification vs CWM\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"Exact Match\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"4B\", \"78.3\", \"72.1\", \"76.2\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"8B\", \"81.5\", \"75.8\", \"79.4\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"4B\", \"69.8\", \"63.4\", \"67.5\", \"31.2%\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"8B\", \"73.2\", \"67.1\", \"71.0\", \"42.7%\"]\n      - name: \"Table 13: CWM Failure Mode Breakdown (4B)\"\n        columns: [\"Failure Mode\", \"% Affected Tests\", \"F1 When Affected\", \"F1 When Unaffected\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Token-budget exhaustion\", \"23.5%\", \"52.1\", \"78.6\"]\n          - [\"String-value error\", \"18.3%\", \"58.7\", \"79.2\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"4.2%\", \"41.3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Neither\", \"62.4%\", \"79.2\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing CLS vs CWM F1 at function-level (no gap) and repo-level (~8.5pp gap), visually showing the complexity-dependent advantage\"\n      - \"Pie chart of CWM failure mode distribution at repo-level\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=output length (tokens), y=CWM exact match rate, showing cliff at ~200 tokens\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 paper 的核心结果。Function-level gap <0.5pp → repo-level gap ~8.5pp，\n      清晰展示 complexity-dependent advantage。CWM failure mode breakdown \n      提供了 mechanistic explanation：不是 classification \"更容易\"，\n      而是 CWM 在 complex output 上遇到了 fundamental 的 generation 瓶颈。\n      CWM 在 \"neither failure mode\" 的 62.4% cases 上达到 79.2 F1——\n      接近 classification——进一步证明 gap 来自 failure modes 而非 \n      inherent task difficulty。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory-level 和 per-test 两种模式，\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的 reference points。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_traj_accuracy: 62.3\n      qwen_8b_traj_f1: 58.7\n      qwen_8b_pertest_pass_f1: 71.2\n      qwen_8b_pertest_fail_f1: 64.5\n      qwen_32b_traj_accuracy: 68.1\n      qwen_32b_traj_f1: 65.4\n      qwen_32b_pertest_pass_f1: 76.3\n      qwen_32b_pertest_fail_f1: 70.8\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_32b_gap: 11.2\n      tokens_per_instance_8b: 1847\n      tokens_per_instance_32b: 2134\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 缺乏 task-specific adaptation，主要依赖 \n      pretrained code understanding。8B zero-shot 显著低于 4B fine-tuned \n      （58.7 vs 87.5 traj F1），因为 fine-tuning 提供了 task format \n      和 evaluation criteria 的精确对齐。32B zero-shot 好于 8B 但仍远低于 \n      4B fine-tuned（65.4 vs 87.5），证明 fine-tuning 的 value 远大于 \n      8× model size scaling。Per-test mode 在两种 size 上均优于 traj mode \n      （8B: 67.9 vs 62.3; 32B: 73.6 vs 68.1），为 classification reformulation \n      提供了额外的 zero-shot evidence。这些 data points 锚定 Pareto frontier \n      的 \"high cost, moderate accuracy\" 区域。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: LLM-as-Judge Baselines vs Fine-tuned Models\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Method\", \"Traj Acc\", \"Per-test Pass F1\", \"Per-test Fail F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B zero-shot\", \"Judge\", \"62.3\", \"71.2\", \"64.5\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B zero-shot\", \"Judge\", \"68.1\", \"76.3\", \"70.8\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B fine-tuned\", \"CLS\", \"87.5*\", \"87.1*\", \"87.9*\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B fine-tuned\", \"CWM\", \"87.5*\", \"87.3*\", \"87.7*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: x=inference cost (tokens), y=accuracy; fine-tuned models dominate zero-shot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuning 4B > zero-shot 32B 是一个 strong practical finding：\n      8× 参数不能弥补 task-specific training 的缺失。\n      Zero-shot per-test > zero-shot traj 进一步支持 classification reformulation \n      的 universality——即使在 zero-shot setting 也有优势。\n      (* 标注 function-level 数字；repo-level fine-tuned 数字见 Table 12)\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      K=3 majority voting with classification model，检验 self-consistency \n      是否提升 per-test accuracy。\n    expected_results:\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      k3_fail_f1: 89.0\n      k3_accuracy: 88.6\n      single_pass_f1: 87.1\n      single_fail_f1: 87.9\n      improvement_from_voting: 1.1\n      agreement_rate_k3: 0.91\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 通过 aggregating 3 次 stochastic forward pass \n      减少 random prediction errors。Classification 的 1-token output \n      使 voting 特别高效（3× cost 仍远低于 CWM 单次 cost）。\n      预测 ~1.1pp 提升是因为 classification 已在 87-88% F1，\n      接近 4B 模型在此 task 上的 ceiling——voting 主要修正 \n      low-confidence boundary cases，对 high-confidence predictions \n      无影响。Agreement rate 91% 表明大多数 prediction 已经 stable。\n      这是一个 P2 实验，提供 practical engineering insight 而非 \n      core claim 支撑。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Majority Voting Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"K\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Cost Multiplier\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"1\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"1×\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"3\", \"88.3\", \"89.0\", \"3×\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"1\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"~35×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing K=1 vs K=3 for CLS, with CWM K=1 cost overlaid\"\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 带来 modest 但 consistent 的提升（+1.1pp），且由于 classification \n      的 1-token inference，3× voting 的总 token cost 仍远低于 CWM 单次 \n      generation（3 tokens vs ~35 tokens）。这提供了一个 Pareto-dominant \n      operating point：CLS K=3 > CWM K=1 in both accuracy and cost。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22222,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22222},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a2813a-ede9-44c9-b128-12e272d1c1ce","uuid":"6d570ca0-37db-4985-a0ba-47868aa8cbe2"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":232968,"duration_api_ms":235433,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完整成立。Function-level null result 通过 multi-seed 确认为 robust，\n  trace-then-judge 证明优势来自 reformulation 而非显式推理。Repo-level 实验中 CWM \n  因 token-budget exhaustion 和 string-value 错误显著落后 classification（~10pp gap），\n  验证 complexity-dependent advantage。Diagnostic re-repair 带来 ~10% resolve rate 提升，\n  block-correlated error structure 实证确认。三条 claim 全部成立，投稿 EMNLP 2026 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification (mvp-b) 和 CWM baseline 各跑 seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean ± std F1，\n      paired bootstrap CI 检验显著性。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.05\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.22\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.88\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.18\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.28\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.31\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.65\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 0.27\n      f1_gap_cls_minus_cwm_pass: -0.23\n      f1_gap_cls_minus_cwm_fail: 0.23\n      paired_bootstrap_p_value: 0.71\n      overlap_95ci: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Function-level 任务的 execution output 短（通常 <20 tokens），CWM 的 token-budget \n      和 string-value 失败模式几乎不触发（exact_match 84% 已经很高）。两种 formulation \n      在信息论上等价：pass/fail 是 output 的确定性函数，模型容量足以学到等效映射。\n      三个 seed 的 std 在 0.2-0.3pp 范围内，符合 4B LoRA 在 ~1890 测试样本上的 \n      expected sampling variance（binomial SE ≈ 0.7pp，LoRA init variance 贡献 ~0.2pp）。\n      p=0.71 远高于 0.05，确认 null result 不是单次运气。这为 repo-level 的 \n      complexity-dependent advantage 提供干净的 baseline：function-level 等价是前提。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Function-Level Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Seed\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"0\", \"86.8\", \"88.1\", \"87.3\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"1\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.6\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"42\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"mean±std\", \"87.05±0.22\", \"87.88±0.18\", \"87.47±0.13\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"0\", \"86.9\", \"87.4\", \"87.1\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"1\", \"87.6\", \"87.9\", \"87.8\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"42\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"mean±std\", \"87.28±0.31\", \"87.65±0.27\", \"87.47±0.29\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing F1 distribution across 3 seeds for CLS vs CWM, 95% CI heavily overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Null result robust：三种子方差 <0.5pp，bootstrap CI 完全重叠。\n      这排除了 \"classification trivially easier\" 的 reviewer concern——\n      在 function-level，两种 formulation 的信息瓶颈相同。\n      CWM 略高的 std（0.31 vs 0.22）暗示 generation 对初始化更敏感，\n      但差异不显著。该结果直接支撑 Claim 1 的前半部分。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单一 Qwen3-4B 模型训练为先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。\n      与直接 classification 对比，检验显式推理是否有帮助。\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 86.1\n      ttj_fail_f1: 86.4\n      ttj_accuracy: 86.2\n      ttj_minus_direct_pass_f1: -0.95\n      ttj_minus_direct_fail_f1: -1.49\n      trace_avg_tokens: 47.3\n      unparseable_rate_pct: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-judge 要求模型在同一 forward pass 中既做 execution reasoning \n      又做 classification。对 4B 参数模型，额外的 trace generation 引入两个负面效应：\n      (1) LoRA capacity 分流——部分参数用于学习 trace 的 surface form 而非 \n      code-test 语义对齐；(2) error propagation——trace 中的推理错误（如变量值 \n      跟踪错误）可能污染后续 pass/fail 判断。在 function-level 这种 \"答案明确\" \n      的设置下，explicit reasoning 不提供额外信息增益（模型已能从 code+test \n      直接推断结果），反而增加了 sequence length 和 loss 分配的竞争。\n      预测 F1 下降 ~1pp，在 best tier 范围 [-2.0, 0.0] 内。\n      这直接证明 reformulation（将 generation 转为 classification）才是关键驱动力，\n      而非 \"跳过推理\" 这一表面简化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"Avg Output Tokens\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Direct Classification\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\", \"1\"]\n          - [\"Trace-then-Judge\", \"86.1\", \"86.4\", \"86.2\", \"48.3\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\", \"34.7\"]\n          - [\"Δ (TtJ − Direct)\", \"-1.0\", \"-1.5\", \"-1.3\", \"+47.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing three methods (Direct CLS, TtJ, CWM) on Pass/Fail F1, showing TtJ slightly below both others\"\n      - \"Example trace outputs showing correct reasoning leading to correct verdict vs incorrect variable tracking leading to wrong verdict\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-judge ≤ direct classification，确认 reformulation \n      而非 explicit reasoning 是 classification 的优势来源。\n      这回应了 \"classification 只是跳过了有用的推理步骤\" 的潜在质疑——\n      加回推理步骤反而有害。值得注意的是 CWM 也不输于 TtJ，\n      说明 CWM 的 generation 过程本身隐含了 execution reasoning，\n      但在 function-level 这一优势被 short output 的 trivial prediction 抵消。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练为预测 resolved/unresolved（trajectory-level），\n      用 aggregated test labels 构造数据。隔离 granularity effect。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 85.3\n      traj_resolved_f1: 84.1\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 86.2\n      traj_resolved_precision: 82.7\n      traj_resolved_recall: 85.5\n      traj_unresolved_precision: 87.4\n      traj_unresolved_recall: 85.1\n      per_test_aggregated_traj_accuracy: 86.8\n      granularity_gap_pct: 1.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 模型将所有 tests 拼接为单一输入，预测 binary resolved/unresolved。\n      相比 per-test 模型，它面临两个劣势：(1) 输入长度显著增加（多个 test 拼接），\n      稀释了对单个 test 的注意力；(2) label 是 all-or-nothing（任一 test fail 则 \n      unresolved），丢失了 \"哪个 test 失败\" 的细粒度信号。在 function-level 数据中 \n      多数 problem 只有 1-3 个 test，所以劣势不大（~1.5pp gap）。但关键发现是 \n      per-test 模型通过 aggregation（majority vote over per-test predictions）可以 \n      recover trajectory-level 判断，反之不行——trajectory-level 无法提供 diagnostic \n      信号。这为 Claim 2 提供了 granularity 的信息论论证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Per-Test vs Trajectory-Level Granularity\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Task\", \"Accuracy\", \"Resolved F1\", \"Unresolved F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Per-Test CLS\", \"per-test pass/fail\", \"87.5\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Per-Test CLS → aggregated\", \"trajectory resolved\", \"86.8\", \"85.9\", \"87.5\"]\n          - [\"Trajectory-Level\", \"trajectory resolved\", \"85.3\", \"84.1\", \"86.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diagram showing information flow: per-test → aggregate = trajectory, but trajectory ↛ per-test\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test 模型 aggregated 后比直接训练的 trajectory-level 模型高 1.5pp，\n      证明细粒度 supervision 提供了更好的学习信号。更重要的是 per-test \n      是 strictly more informative：可以 aggregate 到 trajectory-level，\n      还能提供 diagnostic 信息，而 trajectory-level 无法分解。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      将 classification 和 CWM 模型从 4B 扩展到 8B，检验 function-level \n      equivalence 是否在更大模型上依然成立。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.4\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.1\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 89.7\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.1\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 89.5\n      cls_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.2\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain: 2.0\n      gap_8b_cls_minus_cwm: 0.2\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型在 function-level 上两种 formulation 均提升 ~2pp（log-linear scaling），\n      但 gap 依然 <0.5pp。原因同 multi-seed：function-level output 短，CWM 的 \n      failure modes 不触发。8B 的额外 capacity 均匀地提升了 code semantics 理解，\n      两种 formulation 同等受益。exact_match 从 84% 提升到 87%，说明更大模型 \n      能更精确地预测 output string，但这在 function-level 上不转化为 F1 优势。\n      这个结果强化了 \"gap 是 complexity-dependent 而非 capacity-dependent\" 的论点——\n      需要 repo-level 的复杂 output 才能拉开差距。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Model Size Scaling\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"CWM Exact Match\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"4B\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"87.5\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"8B\", \"89.4\", \"90.1\", \"89.7\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"4B\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"87.5\", \"84.0%\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"8B\", \"89.1\", \"89.8\", \"89.5\", \"87.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=model size (4B, 8B), y=F1, two lines (CLS, CWM) nearly parallel and overlapping\"\n    analysis: >\n      Function-level equivalence 在 8B 维持（gap 0.2pp），排除了 \n      \"4B 太小所以 CWM 被 capacity bottleneck 惩罚\" 的替代解释。\n      Scaling 曲线几乎平行，表明两种 formulation 的 scaling exponent 一致。\n      结合 repo-level 结果（gap ~10pp），这证明 advantage 的触发条件是 \n      task complexity 而非 model capacity。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      在 200 个 SWE-bench 实例上对比：repair agent + per-test failure predictions \n      vs repair agent + trajectory-level binary only。衡量 resolve rate 差异。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate_pct: 28.5\n      diagnostic_resolve_rate_pct: 38.0\n      resolve_delta_pct: 9.5\n      resolve_delta_ci_95: [5.2, 13.8]\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 32\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 13\n      net_improvement_instances: 19\n      avg_repair_iterations_baseline: 3.2\n      avg_repair_iterations_diagnostic: 2.4\n      diagnostic_precision_on_helped: 0.78\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-test failure predictions 提供了 \"哪个 test 失败\" 的 targeted 信息，\n      使 repair agent 能聚焦于特定失败点而非盲目搜索。在 best tier 下预测 \n      ~9.5% 的 resolve rate 提升（range [5, 15]）。提升来源：(1) 多 F2P test \n      实例中，agent 知道具体失败 test 后可优先修复最关键的失败；(2) 减少了 \n      repair iteration 次数（3.2 → 2.4），因为 diagnostic 信号缩小了搜索空间。\n      有 13 个实例 diagnostic 反而有害，主要因 false positive failure predictions \n      误导 agent 去修复没有 broken 的部分。但 net 正向（19 instances），\n      且 95% CI 不包含 0，统计显著。这直接验证了 Claim 2。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Diagnostic Re-repair Results\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Resolve Rate\", \"Avg Iterations\", \"N\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline (binary only)\", \"28.5%\", \"3.2\", \"200\"]\n          - [\"+ Diagnostic per-test\", \"38.0%\", \"2.4\", \"200\"]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+9.5% [5.2, 13.8]\", \"-0.8\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 8: Diagnostic Impact Breakdown\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"Count\", \"Pct\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Diagnostic helped (unresolved → resolved)\", \"32\", \"16.0%\"]\n          - [\"Diagnostic hurt (resolved → unresolved)\", \"13\", \"6.5%\"]\n          - [\"No change\", \"155\", \"77.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: baseline vs diagnostic resolve rates, broken down by F2P test count (T=1, T≥2)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=per-test prediction accuracy on instance, y=whether diagnostic helped\"\n    analysis: >\n      9.5% resolve rate 提升统计显著（CI 不含 0）。提升集中在 T≥2 实例 \n      （与 Claim 3 oracle 分析一致）。Iteration 减少 25% 意味着即使 \n      resolve rate 不变，diagnostic 也有 efficiency value。\n      Hurt cases 主要源于 false positive predictions（precision ~78%），\n      提示 per-test accuracy 仍有改善空间。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure prediction 的 precision/recall，\n      评估 diagnostic 信号质量（不依赖下游执行）。\n    expected_results:\n      failure_precision: 0.876\n      failure_recall: 0.882\n      failure_f1: 0.879\n      pass_precision: 0.874\n      pass_recall: 0.868\n      pass_f1: 0.871\n      macro_f1: 0.875\n      per_problem_perfect_prediction_rate: 0.71\n      per_problem_at_least_one_correct_fail: 0.93\n      confusion_matrix: {TP: 835, FP: 118, FN: 117, TN: 820}\n    result_rationale: >\n      这些数字直接来自 mvp-b-train 的已有结果（pass F1 87.1, fail F1 87.9），\n      此实验是将其分解为 per-problem 粒度的分析。71% 的 problem 所有 test \n      prediction 完全正确——这些 instance 的 diagnostic 信号完全可靠。\n      93% 的 problem 至少有一个 failing test 被正确识别——即使不完美，\n      diagnostic 信号仍有 partial value。Failure precision 87.6% 意味着 \n      每 8 个 predicted-fail 中约 1 个是 false alarm，这与 re-repair 实验中 \n      diagnostic hurt 的比例一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Per-Test Diagnostic Signal Quality\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Failure Precision\", \"0.876\"]\n          - [\"Failure Recall\", \"0.882\"]\n          - [\"Per-problem perfect prediction\", \"71%\"]\n          - [\"Per-problem ≥1 correct fail detected\", \"93%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-recall curve for failure detection at different classification thresholds\"\n      - \"Histogram of per-problem prediction accuracy (fraction of tests correctly predicted)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic 信号质量足以支撑 downstream re-repair：93% 的 problem \n      至少检测到一个真正的 failing test。Per-problem perfect prediction \n      71% 设定了 diagnostic re-repair 的理论上限——对这些 instance，\n      agent 获得完美的 test-level 指引。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T=3+) 分层的 oracle 分析，\n      展示 per-test advantage 集中在 multi-test 实例。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 15.8\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.5\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.298\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.441\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.102\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.219\n    result_rationale: >\n      Oracle simulation 的数学结构决定了 per-test advantage 随 T 单调递增。\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory-level 信息论等价（只有一个 test，\n      pass/fail = resolved/unresolved），advantage 仅来自 tie-breaking \n      在 block-correlated 场景下的微小收益（~0.11）。T=2 时 per-test \n      可以区分 \"两个 test 都 fail\" vs \"一个 pass 一个 fail\"，提供了 \n      trajectory-level 无法获得的额外信息，advantage 跳升至 ~0.19/0.36。\n      T≥3 进一步放大。关键 insight：虽然 T≥2 只占 31.3% 的 SWE-bench 实例，\n      但这些实例贡献了绝大部分 per-test advantage。这提供了 practical \n      decision framework：per-test simulation 值得部署在 multi-test 实例上。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Per-Test Advantage Stratified by F2P Count\"\n        columns: [\"F2P Count\", \"% Instances\", \"IID Advantage\", \"Block Advantage\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"68.7%\", \"0.020\", \"0.109\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"15.8%\", \"0.185\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"15.5%\", \"0.298\", \"0.441\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", \"100%\", \"0.102\", \"0.219\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: x=T bucket, y=advantage, two bars per group (IID, Block)\"\n      - \"Cumulative advantage curve: x=instances sorted by T descending, y=cumulative per-test advantage contribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      T≥2 实例虽然只占 31.3%，但在 block model 下贡献了 \n      (0.362×15.8 + 0.441×15.5) / (0.219×100) ≈ 57% 的总 advantage。\n      这为 selective deployment 提供了明确的 decision boundary：\n      对 T=1 实例可以用 trajectory-level（更简单），\n      对 T≥2 实例部署 per-test verification。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练模型的 test-level predictions 中测量实际 error correlation structure，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-correlated simulation 模型对比。\n    expected_results:\n      empirical_within_instance_error_corr: 0.28\n      iid_model_expected_corr: 0.0\n      block_model_fitted_corr: 0.25\n      block_model_r_squared: 0.87\n      iid_model_r_squared: 0.43\n      residual_heterogeneity: 0.04\n      n_instances_measured: 350\n    result_rationale: >\n      同一 problem_id 下的 tests 共享 code context，模型对该 code 的 \n      \"理解深度\" 产生 instance-level 的 systematic error component。\n      如果模型对某段代码的语义理解有偏差，该 problem 下所有 test 的 \n      prediction 都会系统性偏移——这正是 block correlation 的来源。\n      r=0.28 在 best tier range [0.15, 0.4] 内，表明真实 error structure \n      显著非 i.i.d.（i.i.d. R²=0.43 远低于 block R²=0.87）。\n      Block model 能解释 87% 的 variance，验证了 oracle simulation \n      中使用 block model 的假设。Residual heterogeneity 0.04 表明 \n      block model 不完美但已足够好。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Error Correlation Model Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Expected ρ\", \"Observed ρ\", \"R²\", \"AIC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"I.I.D.\", \"0.00\", \"—\", \"0.43\", \"1247\"]\n          - [\"Block-Correlated\", \"0.25\", \"0.28\", \"0.87\", \"892\"]\n          - [\"Empirical\", \"—\", \"0.28\", \"1.00\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=instance ID (sorted by per-instance error rate), y=per-test error indicator, showing clustering within instances\"\n      - \"QQ plot comparing empirical advantage distribution against IID and block simulation predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Empirical r=0.28 接近 block model 的 fitted r=0.25，远离 i.i.d. 的 0.0。\n      Block model R²=0.87 vs i.i.d. R²=0.43，AIC 差异 355 点，\n      提供了强有力的 model selection 证据。这验证了 oracle simulation \n      的核心假设，也解释了为什么 per-test advantage 在实践中 \n      比 i.i.d. 预测更大。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Per-Test Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels，\n      构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_instances: 467\n      failed_docker_instances: 33\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 89280\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 12.0\n      avg_f2p_tests: 2.8\n      avg_p2p_tests: 9.2\n      label_distribution_pass_pct: 73.5\n      label_distribution_fail_pct: 26.5\n      median_test_code_tokens: 847\n      median_patch_code_tokens: 312\n      docker_total_cpu_hours: 19.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      500 个 SWE-bench Verified 实例中 ~93% 成功提取 per-test labels，\n      33 个失败主要因 Docker 环境问题（依赖版本冲突、timeout）。\n      每个 instance 平均 12 个 test（2.8 F2P + 9.2 P2P），16 个 candidates \n      产生 ~89K 对 (code, test, label)。Pass 率 73.5% 反映了大多数 candidate \n      能通过大多数 P2P tests 但 fail 一些 F2P tests。这个数据集的 class \n      imbalance（73.5/26.5）比 function-level（~52/48）更极端，\n      会成为 repo-level training 的挑战。CPU 消耗 ~19h 符合 16 parallel \n      containers 的预算。该数据集本身是 resource contribution。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: SWE-bench-PerTest Dataset Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instances (successful)\", \"467\"]\n          - [\"Candidates per instance\", \"16\"]\n          - [\"Total (code, test, label) pairs\", \"89,280\"]\n          - [\"Avg F2P tests / instance\", \"2.8\"]\n          - [\"Avg P2P tests / instance\", \"9.2\"]\n          - [\"Pass/Fail ratio\", \"73.5% / 26.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of test count distribution across instances\"\n      - \"Histogram of F2P vs P2P test count distribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集成功构建，467 instances 足以做 train/val/test split（如 350/50/67）。\n      Class imbalance 提示 repo-level training 需要 weighted loss 或 \n      oversampling 策略。F2P 平均 2.8 tests 意味着 31% 多 F2P test 实例 \n      的 oracle 分析在此数据上直接适用。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training & Evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上 fine-tune Qwen3-4B/8B 做 repo-level \n      per-test classification 和 CWM generation，评估 complexity-dependent advantage。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_pass_f1: 78.3\n      cls_4b_fail_f1: 72.1\n      cls_4b_accuracy: 76.2\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 81.5\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 75.8\n      cls_8b_accuracy: 79.4\n      cwm_4b_pass_f1: 69.8\n      cwm_4b_fail_f1: 63.4\n      cwm_4b_accuracy: 67.5\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 73.2\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 67.1\n      cwm_8b_accuracy: 71.0\n      repo_f1_gap_4b_cls_minus_cwm: 8.7\n      repo_f1_gap_8b_cls_minus_cwm: 8.4\n      cwm_4b_exact_match: 31.2\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 42.7\n      cwm_token_budget_exhaustion_pct: 23.5\n      cwm_string_value_error_pct: 18.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level 是整个 paper story 的关键验证点。Classification 在 repo-level \n      仍然只需预测 1 token (pass/fail)，但 CWM 现在需要预测长 execution output \n      （median ~847 tokens 的 test 产生更长的 output）。两个 failure modes 爆发：\n      (1) Token-budget exhaustion（23.5%）：output 超过 generation context window \n      被截断，导致 exact match 失败，模型被迫在 truncated output 上做判断；\n      (2) String-value prediction errors（18.3%）：repo-level output 包含路径、\n      hash、timestamp 等不可预测的 string values，即使逻辑正确也会 mismatch。\n      两者合计影响 ~40% 的 test cases，直接解释了 CWM 的 ~8.5pp F1 drop。\n      Classification 不受这些 failure modes 影响——它只需从 code+test 的语义 \n      推断 pass/fail，不需要重建 output string。8B 模型缩小了部分差距 \n      （exact match 31.2% → 42.7%），但 gap 仍 >8pp，证明这不是 capacity 问题 \n      而是 formulation 的 fundamental limitation。\n      cls_pass_f1 在 [75, 85] range 内（78.3/81.5），repo_f1_gap 在 [5, 15] \n      range 内（8.7/8.4），完全符合 best tier 定义。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 12: Repo-Level Classification vs CWM\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Size\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Accuracy\", \"Exact Match\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"4B\", \"78.3\", \"72.1\", \"76.2\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"8B\", \"81.5\", \"75.8\", \"79.4\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"4B\", \"69.8\", \"63.4\", \"67.5\", \"31.2%\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"8B\", \"73.2\", \"67.1\", \"71.0\", \"42.7%\"]\n      - name: \"Table 13: CWM Failure Mode Breakdown (4B)\"\n        columns: [\"Failure Mode\", \"% Affected Tests\", \"F1 When Affected\", \"F1 When Unaffected\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Token-budget exhaustion\", \"23.5%\", \"52.1\", \"78.6\"]\n          - [\"String-value error\", \"18.3%\", \"58.7\", \"79.2\"]\n          - [\"Both\", \"4.2%\", \"41.3\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Neither\", \"62.4%\", \"79.2\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing CLS vs CWM F1 at function-level (no gap) and repo-level (~8.5pp gap), visually showing the complexity-dependent advantage\"\n      - \"Pie chart of CWM failure mode distribution at repo-level\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=output length (tokens), y=CWM exact match rate, showing cliff at ~200 tokens\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 paper 的核心结果。Function-level gap <0.5pp → repo-level gap ~8.5pp，\n      清晰展示 complexity-dependent advantage。CWM failure mode breakdown \n      提供了 mechanistic explanation：不是 classification \"更容易\"，\n      而是 CWM 在 complex output 上遇到了 fundamental 的 generation 瓶颈。\n      CWM 在 \"neither failure mode\" 的 62.4% cases 上达到 79.2 F1——\n      接近 classification——进一步证明 gap 来自 failure modes 而非 \n      inherent task difficulty。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory-level 和 per-test 两种模式，\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的 reference points。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_8b_traj_accuracy: 62.3\n      qwen_8b_traj_f1: 58.7\n      qwen_8b_pertest_pass_f1: 71.2\n      qwen_8b_pertest_fail_f1: 64.5\n      qwen_32b_traj_accuracy: 68.1\n      qwen_32b_traj_f1: 65.4\n      qwen_32b_pertest_pass_f1: 76.3\n      qwen_32b_pertest_fail_f1: 70.8\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_32b_gap: 11.2\n      tokens_per_instance_8b: 1847\n      tokens_per_instance_32b: 2134\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 缺乏 task-specific adaptation，主要依赖 \n      pretrained code understanding。8B zero-shot 显著低于 4B fine-tuned \n      （58.7 vs 87.5 traj F1），因为 fine-tuning 提供了 task format \n      和 evaluation criteria 的精确对齐。32B zero-shot 好于 8B 但仍远低于 \n      4B fine-tuned（65.4 vs 87.5），证明 fine-tuning 的 value 远大于 \n      8× model size scaling。Per-test mode 在两种 size 上均优于 traj mode \n      （8B: 67.9 vs 62.3; 32B: 73.6 vs 68.1），为 classification reformulation \n      提供了额外的 zero-shot evidence。这些 data points 锚定 Pareto frontier \n      的 \"high cost, moderate accuracy\" 区域。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 14: LLM-as-Judge Baselines vs Fine-tuned Models\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Method\", \"Traj Acc\", \"Per-test Pass F1\", \"Per-test Fail F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B zero-shot\", \"Judge\", \"62.3\", \"71.2\", \"64.5\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B zero-shot\", \"Judge\", \"68.1\", \"76.3\", \"70.8\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B fine-tuned\", \"CLS\", \"87.5*\", \"87.1*\", \"87.9*\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-4B fine-tuned\", \"CWM\", \"87.5*\", \"87.3*\", \"87.7*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: x=inference cost (tokens), y=accuracy; fine-tuned models dominate zero-shot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuning 4B > zero-shot 32B 是一个 strong practical finding：\n      8× 参数不能弥补 task-specific training 的缺失。\n      Zero-shot per-test > zero-shot traj 进一步支持 classification reformulation \n      的 universality——即使在 zero-shot setting 也有优势。\n      (* 标注 function-level 数字；repo-level fine-tuned 数字见 Table 12)\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      K=3 majority voting with classification model，检验 self-consistency \n      是否提升 per-test accuracy。\n    expected_results:\n      k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      k3_fail_f1: 89.0\n      k3_accuracy: 88.6\n      single_pass_f1: 87.1\n      single_fail_f1: 87.9\n      improvement_from_voting: 1.1\n      agreement_rate_k3: 0.91\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 通过 aggregating 3 次 stochastic forward pass \n      减少 random prediction errors。Classification 的 1-token output \n      使 voting 特别高效（3× cost 仍远低于 CWM 单次 cost）。\n      预测 ~1.1pp 提升是因为 classification 已在 87-88% F1，\n      接近 4B 模型在此 task 上的 ceiling——voting 主要修正 \n      low-confidence boundary cases，对 high-confidence predictions \n      无影响。Agreement rate 91% 表明大多数 prediction 已经 stable。\n      这是一个 P2 实验，提供 practical engineering insight 而非 \n      core claim 支撑。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 15: Majority Voting Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"K\", \"Pass F1\", \"Fail F1\", \"Cost Multiplier\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Classification\", \"1\", \"87.1\", \"87.9\", \"1×\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"3\", \"88.3\", \"89.0\", \"3×\"]\n          - [\"CWM Generation\", \"1\", \"87.3\", \"87.7\", \"~35×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing K=1 vs K=3 for CLS, with CWM K=1 cost overlaid\"\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 带来 modest 但 consistent 的提升（+1.1pp），且由于 classification \n      的 1-token inference，3× voting 的总 token cost 仍远低于 CWM 单次 \n      generation（3 tokens vs ~35 tokens）。这提供了一个 Pareto-dominant \n      operating point：CLS K=3 > CWM K=1 in both accuracy and cost。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"16a2813a-ede9-44c9-b128-12e272d1c1ce","total_cost_usd":0.44712949999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22222,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12105,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12105,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5517,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005607,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12105,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":22222,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4415225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b492e0b6-2111-4271-8c96-568023e0237d"}
